{{About|the ground effect|the skill|Shock Ground}}
{{status
| name                   = Shocked Ground
| type                   = Debuff
| icon = Shock status icon.png
| description = You take increased damage while standing on shocked ground
}}
[[File:Shocking ground.jpg|thumb|The visual of a Shocked ground prior game version 3.10]]
'''Shocked ground''' is a detrimental [[ground effect]] that inflicts a debuff that causing affected targets to take increased [[damage]] from all sources. Unless otherwise specified, it has a base Shock value of 15%.

==Mechanics==
Shocked ground applies a flat value of #% increased damage taken. Its default value is 15%, with shocked ground from map mods applying 20%, 35%, or 50% in white, yellow, or red maps respectively. The magnitude of the map mod may further scale with {{c|mod|#% increased effect of Modifiers on non-unique Maps}}. 

When created by the character, shock effect will scale with the player's {{c|mod|#% increased effect of ailments}} modifiers.<ref name="AilmentEffect" /> Shocks from shocked ground are not attributed to the creator of the shocked ground; it does not interact with effects that care about {{c|mod|Shocked by you}}, but conversely it ''can'' shock while you have the {{c|mod|Cannot Shock}} stat.

Shocked ground and [[Shock]] do not stack: the strongest damage taken modifier applies.

===Mitigation=== 
The modifiers {{c|mod|Immune to Shock}} and {{c|mod|Cannot be Shocked}} prevent the application of Shock to the character.<ref name="shocked ground and shock"/> {{c|mod|#% chance to Avoid being Shocked}} functions the same way when stacked to 100%. With {{c|mod|Unaffected by Shock}}, the character will be shocked, but the shock debuff will not modify damage taken. 

Because shock from a ground effect has no duration, shocked ground cannot be avoided through 100% reduced duration of ailments. 

==Sources==
