==Skill gems==
{{Drop enabled gem table
|where = (skill.description LIKE "%Shocked Ground%"
  OR skill.stat_text LIKE "%Shocked Ground%")
}}

==Unique items==
{{Drop enabled unique item table
|tables=item_stats
|join=items._pageID=item_stats._pageID
|where=
  item_stats.id LIKE "%shock%ground%" OR item_stats.id LIKE "%wake%of%destruction%ground%lightning%"
|level=1
|large=1
|stat=1
}}

==Related modifiers==
===Item mods===
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=1 AND (mod_stats.id LIKE "%shock%ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocked ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocking ground%")
|spawn_weights=1
}}

===Map mods===
These mods can appear in maps, or in some cases, logbooks and invitations. Read the spawn weight table to identify the mods:
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=5 AND (mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocked ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocking ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%lightning%")
|spawn_weights=1
}}
Note that legacy maps (maps from [[version 3.1.0]] until 3.8.2d) can have above mods, but have an increase damage taken by 1% due to changes in the mod, from "stat id" known as "map_ground_lightning" (value = 1) to "map_ground_lightning_base_magnitude" (value also = 1 instead of current default values of 20/35/50). Using a {{il|Divine Orb}} can apply the current values.
====Legacy map mods====
The following map mods can only be found on legacy map items in permanent leagues:
{{Modifier table
|q_tables = mod_stats, mod_spawn_weights
|q_join = mods._pageID=mod_stats._pageID, mods._pageID=mod_spawn_weights._pageID
|q_where = mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%lightning%" AND domain = 5
|q_having = SUM(mod_spawn_weights.value) = 0
|q_groupBy = mod_spawn_weights._pageID
|stat_text=1
|level=1
|generation_type =1
|spawn_weights=1
}}
Note that the legacy mods do not have magnitude, and use the default value instead.

===Delve area mods===
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=17 AND (mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocked ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocking ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%lightning%")
|spawn_weights=1
}}
===Synthesis area mods===
Synthesis map mods can only appear in Synthesis area
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=18 AND (mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocked ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocking ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%lightning%")
|spawn_weights=1
}}

===Heist area mods===
Heist area mods can only appear in Heist and Grand Heist:
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mods.domain=22 AND (mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocked ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocking ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%lightning%")
|spawn_weights=1
}}
===Misc===
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=(mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocked ground%" OR mods.stat_text LIKE "%shocking ground%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%ground%lightning%")

AND mods.domain NOT LIKE 1
AND mods.domain NOT LIKE 5
AND mods.domain NOT LIKE 17
AND mods.domain NOT LIKE 18
AND mods.domain NOT LIKE 22
|spawn_weights=1
}}

==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.11.0|
* All mention of "shocking ground" in-game has changed to use "shocked ground". {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.10.1f|
* Clarified the magnitudes of Shocking Ground and [[Chilled Ground]] on their relevant map modifiers.{{efn|name=actual change}}  This is solely a description change.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.10.0|
* Improved the appearance of shocked, burning, caustic and chilled ground.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.9.0|
* The default Shock magnitude for effects that apply Shock without damage (such as [[Summon Skitterbots|Skitterbots]]) is now 15% (from 20%).{{efn|name=actual 3.9 change}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.1.0|
* Map mods have also been rebalanced, and every mod now provides increased item rarity, increased item quantity, and increased monster pack size, though the magnitudes are dependent on the difficulty of the mod.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.0.0|
* Shocking ground increases damage taken by a fixed amount of 20%.
}}
{{Version history table row|2.1.0|
* We've made performance improvements to ground effects. They now use considerably less bandwidth and server resources. Disconnections or lockstep stuttering near ground effects should occur far less often.
}}
{{Version history table row|1.2.0|
* Shock and Shocked Ground have been changed so that they cause 50% increased damage taken (rather than 30%) but no longer stack. They do not stack with each other either. "Cannot Be Shocked" now prevents players being affected by either Shocked Ground or Shock itself.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.9|
* Added support for [[Burning ground|ground fire]] and other environmental hazards.
}}
{{Version history table end}}

